1
00:00:00,439 --> 00:00:02,609
(Amy:)It doesn't matter.
The element was found because of you,

2
00:00:02,775 --> 00:00:04,045
(Amy:)and that's groundbreaking.

3
00:00:04,209 --> 00:00:06,749
(Sheldon:)What matters is
the greatest scientific achievement

4
00:00:06,912 --> 00:00:09,052
(Sheldon:)of my life is based on a blunder.

5
00:00:09,214 --> 00:00:11,694
(Sheldon:)I'm not a genius, I'm a fraud.

6
00:00:13,185 --> 00:00:14,395
(Amy:)You know, Sheldon, in neuroscience,

7
00:00:14,553 --> 00:00:16,793
(Amy:)we're forever finding something
in one part of the brain

8
00:00:16,955 --> 00:00:18,055
(Amy:)that we thought was some-place else.

9
00:00:18,223 --> 00:00:22,693
(Sheldon:)Great. Now I'm worse than
a fraud. I'm practically a biologist.

10
00:00:29,735 --> 00:00:31,545
You got to stop beating
yourself up over this.

11
00:00:31,703 --> 00:00:34,043
I mean, you made a mistake,
but it was a happy mistake.

12
00:00:34,206 --> 00:00:36,116
(Sheldon:)There's nothing happy about it.

13
00:00:36,275 --> 00:00:38,725
(Sheldon:)I'm being given credit
that I don't deserve.

14
00:00:38,877 --> 00:00:41,157
(Leonard:)People get things
they don't deserve all the time.

15
00:00:41,947 --> 00:00:43,927
(Leonard:)Look at me with you.

16
00:00:44,550 --> 00:00:47,220
(Sheldon:)No, Leonard, this is going

17
00:00:47,386 --> 00:00:51,666
(Sheldon:)every science classroom, every
periodic table, every textbook.

18
00:00:51,824 --> 00:00:54,664
(Sheldon:)This mistake
will be staring back at me

19
00:00:54,827 --> 00:01:00,027
(Sheldon:)Like that time you let Koothrappali
wax your eyebrows.

